<title>FRANCE: Farmers drape Arc de Triomphe in black.</title>
<headline>Farmers drape Arc de Triomphe in black.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>French farmers draped Paris' Arc de Triomphe in black on Friday in protest against plans to cut European Union grain subsidies.</p>
<p>Puzzled tourists looked on as the protesters hung black plastic streamers from the top of the towering arch celebrating Emperor Napoleon's battle victories.</p>
<p>Police stepped in before the monument was fully covered.</p>
<p>The farmers said they were protesting against plans, to be discussed by EU farm ministers later this month, to cut subsidies to help finance a reform of the beef industry following the &quot;mad cow&quot; crisis.</p>
</text>
